# Python bytecode from the decomp tools (recover.py imports its siblings).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Do NOT add a blanket *.a / *.o / *.lib / *.obj rule. This repository exists
# to preserve BINARIES with no source, and they are intentionally TRACKED:
#   metoolkit/lib.{rel,chk}/**   the MathEngine Karma 1.2.1 drop (*.a, *.lib, *.obj)
#   lab/allobj/*.o               the 153 shipped objects the recovery reads
#   lab/out*/                    the Ghidra dumps
# A global binary-extension ignore would mask these and break the pipeline.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Compiled scratch binaries the lab produced while debugging. Their sources
# (difftest.c, divcol.c, diverge.c, obb_*.c) ARE tracked; the ELF outputs are
# not — nothing reads them and they are ~19 MB of rebuildable i386 binaries.
/lab/dcol32
/lab/dcol32_recovered
/lab/dcol64
/lab/difftest
/lab/difftest_boxbox
/lab/difftest_sse
/lab/div32
/lab/div64

# Local build / scratch trees
/build*/
/_deps/
